WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.077 --> 00:00:03.636
-As President Biden touted
his infrastructure plan

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.704
to create jobs
and stimulate the economy,

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:08.808
one of the signature scams
of the Trump era,

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.743
a deal that was also supposed to

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.678
create jobs
and stimulate the economy,

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.547
fell apart, revealing yet again

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.850
that the GOP's new brand of
supposed pro-worker populism

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.285
is a giant fraud.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.721
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:25.524
♪♪

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.226
Let me just say
right off the bat

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.796
that we are aware that
federal investigators

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:32.031
executed search warrants
of Rudy Giuliani's office

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.466
and apartment this morning,

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.436
and I promise we will have a lot
more to say about it tomorrow

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:40.272
because there is no subject
nearer and dearer to our hearts

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:42.175
than Rudy Giuliani
being a giant [bleep]

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.409
I'm guessing, when they arrived,

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.645
Rudy tried to flush his phone
down the toilet

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.780
as the feds were carrying away
the toilet.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.949
"Sir, it's a floor model.
It's not attached to anything."

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.718
"Oh, no, Rudy, ya dope!

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:55.688
You're supposed to have pipes."

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.923
Also, President Biden
delivered his first address

00:00:57.923 --> 00:00:59.959
to a joint session of Congress
tonight.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.594
And we're taping this
beforehand,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.029
so we don't know what he said,

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.798
but something tells me he had
a slightly different energy

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:08.768
than the speeches he attended
as President Obama's VP,

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:12.104
where he was always doing stuff
like grabbing John Boehner's arm

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:14.440
or giving finger guns
to people in the crowd

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.709
like he was walking around
a villa in Miami Beach

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.145
making sure everyone at
the pool party was having fun.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.948
"Cam, that glass looks empty.
You need a refill?

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.882
Stacy, I better see you
in the pool later.

00:01:23.882 --> 00:01:25.117
I got the jets turned on.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.720
Brad, throw another dog
on the grill for me.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.223
I worked up an appetite kicking
Steve's ass in volleyball.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.258
You got to work on your dig,
Steve."

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.460
One thing we do know
about Biden's speech

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.896
is that he has very likely
spent some time

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.966
touting his infrastructure plan,
and as he pitches that plan,

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.502
he's also dealing with
an intransigent GOP

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.337
that has its own idea
for infrastructure,

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.805
a GOP that's also trying to
rebrand itself

00:01:46.805 --> 00:01:49.475
after decades of subservience
to corporate interests

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.877
as a populist,
pro-workers party.

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:54.079
They've gone from defending
so-called job creators

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:55.948
and decrying class warfare

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.217
to calling corporations
that don't side with them

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:00.386
on cultural issues woke.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.255
-This past month,
we have seen the rise

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:05.491
of the woke corporation.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:08.861
We have seen the rise
of big business

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:13.700
enforcing a woke standard.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.201
-I think corporate America,

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:18.070
by trying to genuflect
to this wokeness,

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.173
I think they have gone down
a really bad road.

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:22.141
They're going to tie themselves
in knots

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:24.510
trying to please
the extreme left.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.545
-Senator McConnell
says corporations

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:29.782
are, quote, behaving like
woke parallel governments

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.684
and becoming like a vehicle
for far-left mobs

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:34.387
to hijack our country.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.355
-Let's just cut to the chase.

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:40.793
The big tech platforms
are owned and operated

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.628
by woke capitalists.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.964
They're leftists.
They're liberals.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.466
-There's no way Mark Zuckerberg
is woke.

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.669
At most, he's switched on.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.504
And none of those Plutocrats
are leftists.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.640
I'm pretty sure Jeff Bezos
and Bernie Sanders

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.576
aren't on the same page when it
comes to most political issues.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.878
I doubt Bernie even uses Amazon.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.281
"I get everything I need
from the co-op,

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:02.982
and when I run out of batteries,

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.651
I just connect some copper wire
to a potato.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.887
Hey, turn down the A/C.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:10.256
Potatoes don't grow on trees."

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.425
And just because

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:15.394
they pulled some Dr. Seuss books
with racist language

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:17.663
and put out statements
against voter suppression laws

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.333
doesn't mean companies
like Amazon and Delta
are suddenly woke.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.601
For one thing, they both
tried to bust unions.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.438
Amazon put up anti-union posters
in employee bathrooms,

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.573
and Delta handed out flyers
that said,

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:30.142
"Union dues cost
around $700 a year.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:33.579
A new video game system with
the latest hits sounds like fun.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:34.948
Put your money towards that

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.649
instead of paying dues
to the union."

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:39.118
Yeah, exactly. And if you
get sick in real life,

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:42.121
all you have to do is
hit a brick with your head
until a mushroom pops out.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.457
The point is, these
giant corporations
aren't suddenly woke

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.492
just because they've done
the bare minimum of, say,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.228
coming out against
racist voter suppression laws.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.430
But Republicans are still
infuriated by that,

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.166
so they've tried to co-opt
the anti-corporate language

00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:55.868
of actual left-wing populists

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.170
like Bernie, Elizabeth Warren,
and AOC.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.807
For example,
Florida Senator Marco Rubio

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.909
wrote an absolutely ludicrous
screed

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.844
against supposedly
woke corporations

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:06.445
in the "New York Post"
this week,

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:09.615
where he said, "No policymaker
would allow a company

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:12.018
to dump toxic waste into a river

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:15.254
upstream of a thriving town
he is charged with governing.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:18.691
Yet corporate America eagerly
dumps woke, toxic nonsense

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.992
into our culture,

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.194
and it's only gotten
more destructive with time.

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:24.630
These campaigns will be met
with the same strength

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.799
that any other polluter
should expect."

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.667
What any other polluter
should expect?

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:31.170
So, basically, total and
complete loyalty from the GOP?

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.439
Republicans cut so many
environmental regulations,

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:34.907
I'm pretty sure
they made it legal

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.476
to sell toxic sludge
as an energy drink.

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:40.647
And do I drink a sludge
every now and then?

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:42.014
Yeah.

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:43.249
That's only because
I'm up all night

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.351
writing this week's corrections.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.053
These guys are, in many way,
just following

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.521
in Donald Trump's footsteps.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.089
He was not in any serious way
a populist,

00:04:51.089 --> 00:04:54.160
except that he co-opted
some of the language of populism

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.095
while doling out trillions
in giveaways

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.897
to corporations that mostly just

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.966
gave the money
to their wealthy investors.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.235
Trump, for example,
said the 2017 tax cuts

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.236
would be rocket fuel
for the economy,

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.906
and earlier this month, Senate
Minority Leader Mitch McConnell

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:09.174
said rolling them back
would destroy jobs.

00:05:09.174 --> 00:05:14.513
-This tax bill of 2017, undone,

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:19.986
would create an extensive loss
of jobs in our country,

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.255
do exactly the wrong thing,

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:24.189
and move us
in the wrong direction.

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:25.924
-You hear that,
woke corporations?

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:27.760
The Republican party
is on to you.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.562
If you don't stop dumping
woke toxic waste

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:32.264
into our cultural river,

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:35.468
then we are going to punish you
by allowing you to...

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:38.137
continue paying zero dollars
in federal income taxes.

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:41.106
That can't be right. Wally,
I think the card is wrong.

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:42.941
-That's what it said
in the script.

00:05:42.941 --> 00:05:44.443
-But does it seem right to you?

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.745
-Hey, Seth, I just write
the cards, baby.

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:48.981
-Wally, the only way
you could be cooler

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.184
is if you wore sunglasses
under your face shield.

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:54.053
Anyway, the point is,
this is the scam.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.555
Republicans call themselves
pro-worker populists

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.824
while doling out cash
to giant companies

00:05:58.824 --> 00:06:01.460
who mostly use it to decrease
their tax liabilities

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.928
and enrich
their wealthy investors,

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.264
even though the whole point
was supposed to be

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:08.568
to use that money to invest
in the economy and create jobs.

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:12.271
And there was a perfect test
case of this scam in Wisconsin

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.106
at the start
of Trump's presidency.

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:17.309
-After months of speculation,
Foxconn promises

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:21.047
to build its first American
factory here in Wisconsin.

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:23.416
-It's the largest
economic development project

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:24.917
in state history

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:29.321
and will initially require more
than 16,000 construction jobs

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:31.858
sourced from
Wisconsin businesses.

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:34.026
The LCD manufacturing campus

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.729
expected to be operational
in 2020

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.364
and the project
expected to have

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:42.802
at least a $7 billion annual
economic impact on the state.

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:44.604
-And with this project
moving forward,

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:46.705
Governor Walker coined
a new term today,

00:06:46.705 --> 00:06:48.141
the Wisconn Valley,

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:51.777
describing our area as a new hub
for technology and innovation.

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:55.113
-They wouldn't have done it here
except that I became president,

00:06:55.113 --> 00:06:56.415
so that's good.

00:06:56.415 --> 00:07:01.520
Congratulations on truly
one of the eighth wonders.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.289
I think we can say this is --

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.358
We can say the eighth wonder
of the world.

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.593
This is the eighth wonder
of the world.

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.829
-Yeah, it goes great pyramids,

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.764
the Colossus of Rhodes,

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.899
and then a factory in Wisconsin.

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:16.368
You get the sense Trump has used
"eighth wonder of the world"

00:07:16.368 --> 00:07:18.537
to describe a lot of his
projects over the years.

00:07:18.537 --> 00:07:20.105
"Trump Taj Mahal --
It's going to be

00:07:20.105 --> 00:07:21.774
the eighth wonder of the world.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.676
Blackjack tables,
cocktail waitresses,

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.777
and we're going to
pump in oxygen

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:27.913
to keep people gambling longer,

00:07:27.913 --> 00:07:31.050
just like the guy
who built the real Taj Mahal,

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.818
the Emperor Shah Jahan.

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:34.720
Great guy. Great guy.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.191
Met him at Studio 54
back in '86.

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:40.259
He was there
with Christie Brinkley.

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:44.663
She went on to marry Billy Joel,
Mr. Piano Guy himself.

00:07:44.663 --> 00:07:47.165
You know, I love the song
'We Didn't Start the Fire,'

00:07:47.165 --> 00:07:49.735
but I always thought
'Trump' should be in that song.

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:52.371
A lot of famous people
in there, but no Trump.

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:55.107
What do we think, folks?
Should Trump be --

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:58.044
Should 'Trump' be in
'We Didn't Start the Fire'?

00:07:58.044 --> 00:08:00.679
Space monkey, Mafia,
Donald Trump --

00:08:00.679 --> 00:08:03.115
Has a nice ring to it.

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:06.118
You don't want to mess with
the space monkey Mafia.

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:10.223
Almost impossible to do
construction on other planets."

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:16.261
"Got to kick back
a lot of space bananas.

00:08:16.261 --> 00:08:18.263
You know, they'll say...

00:08:18.263 --> 00:08:20.533
they'll say Trump
tried to start the fire,

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:22.801
but we know that's not true.

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:25.104
We know that's not true."

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:28.407
The Foxconn deal was supposed to
be the shining example

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:30.409
of Trump's claim that he was
bringing manufacturing jobs

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:31.944
back to the United States,

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:35.114
and it was proof of concept for
the Republican way of doing it,

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:37.283
not by investing directly
in infrastructure

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:39.752
but by doling out subsidies
to big companies.

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:42.288
Trump was even there for
the ground-breaking ceremony

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:44.489
with then Wisconsin Governor
Scott Walker,

00:08:44.489 --> 00:08:46.692
where he picked up some dirt
with a gold shovel

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.995
and then gently tossed it back
on the ground

00:08:49.995 --> 00:08:52.764
near the spot where
he dug it up from.

00:08:52.764 --> 00:08:55.601
"There you go.
I loosened it up for you."

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:57.503
For a guy who was supposedly
in construction,

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:58.938
he doesn't even know
how to fake it.

00:08:58.938 --> 00:09:01.807
If you handed him a hammer, he
would talk it into like a phone.

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:04.076
"Send me your best nail guy."

00:09:04.076 --> 00:09:06.211
Under the deal,
Foxconn was promised

00:09:06.211 --> 00:09:09.281
a stunning $4 billion
in taxpayer subsidies,

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:12.218
and, in return, they were
supposed to spend $10 billion

00:09:12.218 --> 00:09:14.553
employing 13,000 people

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:16.922
at a 20-million-square-foot
manufacturing campus

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:17.990
in Wisconsin

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.758
and instantly
establish Wisconsin

00:09:19.758 --> 00:09:21.727
as a destination
for tech firms.

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.628
Again, this was supposed to be
proof positive

00:09:23.628 --> 00:09:26.365
of Trump's ability to magically
bring back manufacturing jobs

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:28.200
without actually making

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.502
any of the real direct
investments in the economy

00:09:30.502 --> 00:09:32.771
that, say, Joe Biden and the
Democrats are now proposing.

00:09:32.771 --> 00:09:36.075
It was also a distillation
of the core GOP philosophy,

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:37.809
which is that if you
give massive handouts

00:09:37.809 --> 00:09:40.913
to giant businesses that are
already flush with cash

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:43.349
instead of giving the money
directly to workers,

00:09:43.349 --> 00:09:45.984
those handouts will eventually
trickle down and create jobs.

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:49.789
And credit, where it's due,
the plan worked.

00:09:49.789 --> 00:09:51.824
The project has been
a huge success.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:53.960
What's that? It wasn't.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.096
Shoemaker, you got to tell me
this stuff before the show.

00:09:57.096 --> 00:10:00.032
This is not cool.
Wally, are you cool with this?

00:10:00.032 --> 00:10:01.801
-I'm cool with everything,
baby.

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:05.204
-Rock and roll, Wally.
How can I stay mad?

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:08.140
The point is, the Foxconn deal
was a giant scam.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.409
It was obvious it was a scam
from the very beginning.

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:12.978
For one thing,
they kept missing key goals

00:10:12.978 --> 00:10:14.880
and failing to deliver
on their promises,

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.514
cycling from one idea
to the next.

00:10:16.514 --> 00:10:18.718
This is a real summary

00:10:18.718 --> 00:10:21.720
of all the different projects
Foxconn considered for the site.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.690
The company spent years pivoting
wildly from idea to idea.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:27.892
The enormous
Gen 10.5 LCD factory

00:10:27.892 --> 00:10:29.829
specified in the contract

00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:32.164
became a far smaller Gen 6,

00:10:32.164 --> 00:10:33.699
then was canceled,
then came back.

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.901
The company announced
it was building something

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:39.571
called the AI+8K+5G ecosystem

00:10:39.571 --> 00:10:42.374
to be developed in a network
of innovation centers,

00:10:42.374 --> 00:10:45.811
buildings that the company
purchased only to leave empty.

00:10:45.811 --> 00:10:47.546
It looked into building
fish farms,

00:10:47.546 --> 00:10:49.749
exporting ice cream,
storing boats.

00:10:49.749 --> 00:10:52.584
It announced plans to build
coffee kiosks and ventilators

00:10:52.584 --> 00:10:54.185
that never moved forward.

00:10:54.185 --> 00:10:56.288
Most recently, it said it would
build electric cars,

00:10:56.288 --> 00:10:57.890
though maybe,
the company acknowledged,

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.491
that will happen in Mexico.

00:10:59.491 --> 00:11:02.561
Man, that sounds like how I plan
a Mother's Day gift for my wife.

00:11:02.561 --> 00:11:04.229
I'm going to commission
a painting of our family.

00:11:04.229 --> 00:11:05.397
Nope,
I don't have time for that.

00:11:05.397 --> 00:11:06.798
I'm going to take a picture
of our family.

00:11:06.798 --> 00:11:08.166
Nope, ran out of time.

00:11:08.166 --> 00:11:09.668
I'm going to find an existing
picture of our family

00:11:09.668 --> 00:11:11.437
and have it framed.
Nope, I don't have time.

00:11:11.437 --> 00:11:13.272
I'm going find an existing
picture of our family

00:11:13.272 --> 00:11:14.973
and text it her with
"Happy Mother's Day."

00:11:14.973 --> 00:11:16.274
Nope, I'm going to forget
entirely,

00:11:16.274 --> 00:11:17.709
and then I'm gonna wake up
two Sundays from now

00:11:17.709 --> 00:11:19.344
in an empty bed
while it slowly dawns on me

00:11:19.344 --> 00:11:20.912
that I am [bleep]

00:11:20.912 --> 00:11:24.550
"Honey, I built you a place
to store boats."

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:27.019
And yet, as this scam
was unfolding,

00:11:27.019 --> 00:11:29.488
the village where the campus
was supposed to be located

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:31.890
was in the process
of buying up properties

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.692
and building new roads
to make way

00:11:33.692 --> 00:11:35.827
for this fancy new factory
they were promised.

00:11:35.827 --> 00:11:38.264
Wisconsin has already spent
at least $400 million

00:11:38.264 --> 00:11:39.898
on land and infrastructure,

00:11:39.898 --> 00:11:43.034
and as of 2019, the village
where the plant is located

00:11:43.034 --> 00:11:45.537
had paid just over $152 million

00:11:45.537 --> 00:11:47.973
for 132 properties
to make way for Foxconn,

00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:50.943
plus $7.9 million
in relocation costs.

00:11:50.943 --> 00:11:52.378
Meanwhile, Foxconn

00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:54.780
owns a lot of real estate
in southern Wisconsin now,

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.782
and it has built
an odd collection of buildings,

00:11:56.782 --> 00:11:58.983
including the
million-square-foot structure

00:11:58.983 --> 00:12:00.586
it called the LCD Fab

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:02.454
and a glass orb.

00:12:02.454 --> 00:12:04.456
Cool, so now
instead of 13,000 jobs

00:12:04.456 --> 00:12:06.225
building high-tech
LCD displays,

00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:08.527
taxpayers ended up spending
hundreds of millions of dollars

00:12:08.527 --> 00:12:10.596
on a useless glass orb.

00:12:10.596 --> 00:12:12.631
Although, shout-out
to Donald Trump

00:12:12.631 --> 00:12:15.567
on being our first
two-orb President.

00:12:15.567 --> 00:12:18.771
What do you even do with a glass
orb you don't need anymore?

00:12:18.771 --> 00:12:20.873
Turn it into a community center?

00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:22.374
"All right, kids,
it's time for recess.

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:24.777
Everyone line up
outside the glass orb,

00:12:24.777 --> 00:12:27.346
and remember,
do not touch the orb.

00:12:27.346 --> 00:12:30.516
We still don't know what it does
or what its powers are."

00:12:30.516 --> 00:12:33.151
Or maybe they'll use it as
a Packers training facility.

00:12:33.151 --> 00:12:34.620
"All right, go long,
but remember,

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.523
don't run into the glass wall
again."

00:12:37.523 --> 00:12:39.058
But it gets even crazier
than that

00:12:39.058 --> 00:12:40.760
because the state
actually demolished homes

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.828
and built new roads that,
in a metaphor

00:12:42.828 --> 00:12:46.765
that's almost "two" on the nose,
actually lead to nowhere.

00:12:46.765 --> 00:12:48.434
Former President Trump announced

00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:51.603
Foxconn was coming
July 26, 2017.

00:12:51.603 --> 00:12:54.706
The following June, Trump,
former Congressman Paul Ryan,

00:12:54.706 --> 00:12:57.109
and former Governor Scott Walker
were among those

00:12:57.109 --> 00:12:59.578
who broke ground on the plant
in Mount Pleasant.

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:02.080
And since then,
roads have been widened,

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.416
land flattened,
homes demolished,

00:13:04.416 --> 00:13:07.218
and the plant has not built
anything yet.

00:13:07.218 --> 00:13:09.521
-I was there. It's the
weirdest thing, Bertha.

00:13:09.521 --> 00:13:14.126
There's basically
a giant clear dome

00:13:14.126 --> 00:13:18.631
that I think is some kind
of data center/museum,

00:13:18.631 --> 00:13:20.999
a couple of big warehouses,

00:13:20.999 --> 00:13:23.936
and then farms
and some homes down the street.

00:13:23.936 --> 00:13:26.238
It is --
There's a bunch of new roads

00:13:26.238 --> 00:13:28.006
that kind of lead to nowhere.

00:13:28.006 --> 00:13:29.909
-What did they use
for the blueprints,

00:13:29.909 --> 00:13:32.244
an M.C. Escher dorm room poster?

00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:34.947
A giant orb and a bunch of roads
that lead to nowhere.

00:13:34.947 --> 00:13:37.315
This whole thing is starting to
sound like a David Lynch
project.

00:13:37.315 --> 00:13:39.118
Did they also give them
$4 billion

00:13:39.118 --> 00:13:40.553
to build
a state-of-the-art red room

00:13:40.553 --> 00:13:41.953
where a little man in a red suit

00:13:41.953 --> 00:13:43.989
teaches you how to dance
and talk in reverse?

00:13:43.989 --> 00:13:47.226
And even now that Foxconn has
mostly abandoned the project,

00:13:47.226 --> 00:13:49.828
they're still scooping up
taxpayer handouts

00:13:49.828 --> 00:13:52.031
even as they leave behind
a trail of debt,

00:13:52.031 --> 00:13:54.266
broken promises, and chaos.

00:13:54.266 --> 00:13:57.803
Foxconn is still eligible for
$80 million in tax subsidies,

00:13:57.803 --> 00:13:59.371
and under the revised deal,

00:13:59.371 --> 00:14:01.340
the state is still paying
a per-job subsidy

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.874
of about $55,000.

00:14:02.874 --> 00:14:05.076
$55,000 for each job.

00:14:05.076 --> 00:14:07.479
Instead of giving that
to a massive foreign company,

00:14:07.479 --> 00:14:09.381
how about you give that
directly to workers

00:14:09.381 --> 00:14:10.683
to build useful stuff here,

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:12.651
like bridges
and broadband infrastructure,

00:14:12.651 --> 00:14:14.286
instead of roads to nowhere

00:14:14.286 --> 00:14:17.356
and a giant glass orb that's
just going to sit there empty

00:14:17.356 --> 00:14:19.591
and inevitably cause
traffic delays?

00:14:19.591 --> 00:14:22.461
"Honey, I'm going to go to
Kroger to pick up some milk.

00:14:22.461 --> 00:14:24.897
I'll be back in about two hou--
The road leads to nowhere.

00:14:24.897 --> 00:14:26.865
I got to go around
the giant orb.

00:14:26.865 --> 00:14:28.267
What do you mean,
which giant orb?

00:14:28.267 --> 00:14:30.502
The Foxconn orb.

00:14:30.502 --> 00:14:34.139
Turn off the hairdryer if you
want to have this conversation."

00:14:34.139 --> 00:14:36.941
So as Biden talks up
his infrastructure plan

00:14:36.941 --> 00:14:38.510
which would raise
corporate taxes

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:40.645
in order to make
direct investments in workers

00:14:40.645 --> 00:14:42.481
to build things
we actually need,

00:14:42.481 --> 00:14:44.850
the Foxconn scam
is a cautionary tale about

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:47.319
what Republicans would have us
do with that money instead.

00:14:47.319 --> 00:14:49.554
They want to shovel handouts
to giant corporations

00:14:49.554 --> 00:14:51.356
already flush with cash,

00:14:51.356 --> 00:14:53.025
and all the while,
they're ludicrously trying

00:14:53.025 --> 00:14:55.594
to rebrand themselves as a party
of pro-worker populists.

00:14:55.594 --> 00:14:57.929
Say what you will
about a scam like this,

00:14:57.929 --> 00:14:59.398
but one thing's for sure.

00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:02.834
-They wouldn't have done it here
except that I became president.

00:15:02.834 --> 00:15:04.803
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:04.803 --> 00:15:07.972
♪♪

00:15:07.972 --> 00:15:09.274
God's Love We Deliver

00:15:09.274 --> 00:15:11.176
